# Queue jobs

One `email_jobs` row and one queued job per recipient. `QUEUE_CONNECTION=database`. Dispatch only after the campaign transaction commits.

## Do

- Process pending jobs FIFO.
- Simulate the send. Log the campaign id, the recipient, success, and campaign completion.
- Set the email job to `sent` on success and `failed` on failure.
- Move the campaign from `queued` to `processing` to `done`.
- Skip a job that is no longer `pending`.

## Do not

- Call a real mail provider.
- Let one recipient failure stop the worker.
- Treat `done` as "every email succeeded". `done` means every job is `sent` or `failed`.

```php
// ✅ GOOD
if ($emailJob->status !== EmailJobStatus::Pending) {
    return;
}
```
